# Build-context filter for the production Dockerfile.
#
# Two jobs (both load-bearing):
#   1. SECURITY (T-06-01): keep every secret/runtime-state family OUT of the
#      image. config.toml carries the auto-generated API key (D-01); *.db,
#      cloudflare-userdata*/, and *.env carry runtime/secret state. These live
#      ONLY on the /state + /data/manga volumes — never baked into a layer.
#   2. Keep the context small/fast (the Chromium layer is already large).
#
# The build NEEDS pyproject.toml, uv.lock, src/, and README.md — those are NOT
# excluded. Mirrors the secret/state families already in .gitignore.

# ── Secrets / runtime state — MUST NOT be baked (T-06-01) ────────────────────
config.toml
*.db
gateway.db*
cloudflare-userdata/
cloudflare-userdata-*/
comix-userdata/
.env
*.env
.proxytest.env

# ── Python / build caches ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# ── Virtual env / tooling caches ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.nox/
.hypothesis/

# ── Dev / CI / planning trees not needed in the prod image ───────────────────
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.planning/
tests/
docker/

# ── Throwaway diagnostic / recon output ──────────────────────────────────────
_recon_out/
_e2e_out/
local-repro-*.log
junit.xml

# ── Docs not needed at build time (README.md IS needed → re-included below) ──
*.md
!README.md
